toujours malgré le discours officiel","publisher":"AllAfrica / RFI","date":"2026-06-09"},"8":{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202608180670.html","title":"Le Gouvernement confirme des signaux de paix face au phénomène Mobondo !","publisher":"AllAfrica","date":"2026-08-18"}},"units":{"CD3201-bandundu":"Bandundu city, former provincial capital on the Kwilu/Kasai confluence in Kwilu province, is a state-held town with no armed group exercising territorial control. Daily order, arrests and policing across its communes (Basoko, Disasi, Mayoyo) and health-area neighbourhoods are handled by the PNC, with FARDC elements garrisoned in the town. The Mobondo (Teke-Yaka conflict) militia has been active since 2022 in neighbouring Kwamouth (Mai-Ndombe) and in parts of Bagata and other Kwilu territories, prompting FARDC deployments in the region, but it is not reported to hold or regularly operate inside Bandundu city or its periurban villages (Kanga, Station). Web research was largely unavailable (search budget exhausted, sources blocked); regional Mobondo reporting from mid-2026 is cited, but the city assessment rests on default state presence."}}